quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  2,17,"Their parable is that of one who kindled a fire, but as soon as it lit up all around him, Allah took away their light and left them in utter darkness; they do not see."
  2,18,"(They are) deaf, dumb and blind; they shall never return (to the right path)."
  2,19,"Alternatively, (their parable is) that of a rainstorm from the sky, with utter darkness, thunder and lightning. They put their fingers into their ears, fearing death due to the thunderclaps. Allah thus encompasses the disbelievers."
  2,20,"The lightning almost takes away their sight; whenever it flashes upon them, they start walking on, but as soon as darkness falls over them, they stand still. Had Allah willed, He would have taken away their hearing and sight. Indeed, Allah is All-Capable of everything."
  2,21,"O people! Worship your Lord, Who has created you and those before you, perhaps you may become God-conscious."
  2,22,"He Who has made the earth a bed for you and the sky a dome, and sends down rain from the cloud, and with it He brings forth fruits for your sustenance. Therefore, do not set up rivals to Allah knowingly."
  2,23,"If you are in doubt concerning what we have revealed to Our (exalted) servant, produce only one chapter comparable to this Book (the Qur’an). And call upon your helpers (to assist you) besides Allah if you are truthful."
  2,24,"However, if you cannot do so, and you will not, then fear the Fire whose fuel is humans (i.e. the disbelievers) and stones (i.e. their idols), prepared for the disbelievers."
